// registerSwagger mounts the public Swagger surface on the web mux:
//
//   - GET /openapi.yaml → the embedded spec (application/yaml)
//   - GET /openapi.json → the embedded spec (application/json)
//   - GET /docs/*      → Swagger UI (vendored via github.com/swaggo/http-swagger)
//
// These routes are UNAUTHENTICATED (INV-public-contract) — the API contract +
// UI load before any token, like the SPA shell. They are registered ahead of
// the SPA fallback so /openapi.* and /docs never leak index.html.
